# =============================================================================
# Trivy CVE ignore list.
#
# All CVEs suppressed before 2026-04-16 (jaraco.context, wheel, setuptools,
# urllib3, protobuf) were resolved on that date by:
#   - Rebuilding dbt-scheduler on a plain python-slim base (Debian trixie) to
#     replace the Debian 11 bullseye base from dbt-labs/dbt-postgres:1.9.0.
#   - Adding `pip install --upgrade setuptools wheel urllib3 jaraco.context`
#     to all four custom Python images (producer, alert-receiver, kafka-lag,
#     dbt-scheduler) to patch transitive dependencies.
#   - Bumping the Go builder in retention-image to a patched release.
#
# Add new entries below only when a CVE cannot be patched at build time,
# and include: package, brief justification, date added, expected review date.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# pip's vendored dependencies (msgpack, setuptools)
# Added: 2026-08-20
# Expires: 2026-11-20
#
# Both findings come from pip's own `_vendor` directory, not from anything this
# project installs. pip 26.2.1 (the current release, shipped in python:3.14-slim)
# pins msgpack==1.1.2 and setuptools==70.3.0 in src/pip/_vendor/vendor.txt, and
# Trivy reports those pins. The images themselves ship setuptools 84.0.0 and no
# msgpack at all, which the scan output confirms per METADATA file.
#
# Not patchable at build time: `pip install --upgrade` cannot reach a vendored
# copy, and 26.2.1 is the newest release. Neither copy is importable by
# application code and pip is never invoked at runtime.
#
# msgpack: already re-vendored to 1.2.1 on pip's main branch, so this entry
# clears itself with the next pip release. setuptools: still 70.3.0 upstream.
# At review time, check the vendor.txt of the current pip release first.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
